WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.534
-Tig, it's great to see you.
-It's great to see you.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.033
-Yeah, I'm happy you're here.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.734
I have a lot of things to talk
to you about and ask you about.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.434
-Great.
That's what I'm here for.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:09.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.133
-I have one thing I want to ask
you about.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.400
You were recently on a celebrity
"Wheel of Fortune."

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.167
Do you remember this?

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.434
-I do.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.067
-Yeah.
-You had to answer this puzzle.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.234
I'm going to show it
to everyone.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.367
-Okay.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.767
-I don't know how this story
ends really.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.701
This is the puzzle.

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.434
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.467
-That was a puzzle.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:33.801
-Yes. Now, that's -- So you --
"Crashing my..."

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.801
-Do you want to know
what I said?

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.567
-Yeah.
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.334
It must be
"crashing my exercise bike."

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:46.567
-Um, well...

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.400
-Let's see what you said.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.501
-Tig?

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.701
-Crashing my exor...cist bill?

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:55.634
[ Buzzer ]

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.501
Can we edit my guess out?

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.667
"Crashing my exorcist bill."

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.033
That is the answer.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.868
I'm not going to be humiliated
on national television.

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.434
-It's too late for that.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.567
-Now, what was --

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.567
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:13.701
-What was going through your --

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.567
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.133
What was going through your head
at the moment?

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.901
-Well, I mean -- Well, first of
all, I was thinking,

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.300
"I never imagined I'd be on
'Wheel of Fortune.'"

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.334
-Yeah.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.834
-Second of all, I was thinking,

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.734
"I don't imagine
I'll be very good at this."

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.701
And then third, I was like,
"Well, I'm correct."

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:36.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:39.033
-You didn't think it was --
Or were you just being funny?

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.067
You're just being -- No.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.634
-No, I --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.601
-You really thought it was
"exorcist bill."

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.701
-I really was like --
-You're nervous?

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:51.000
-I wasn't nervous.
I was -- You know, I was wrong.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:55.334
I was just wrong.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:02:02.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.367
These people are --

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.601
-I feel like these things happen
to you.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.067
These funny things happen
to you.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.334
I think you're a magnet for
funny things that happen.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.734
And this is another example.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:15.000
This is an article that was
on Buzzfeed.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.934
It says, "an Airbnb host
complained about their booking

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:21.067
being low and people responded
with a list of reasons why they

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.267
refused to use the service,"
Airbnb.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.567
And there's just a photo of you
last time you were on our show.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.467
-Do you know anything about this
or...?

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:33.701
-No. Your producer showed this
to me.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:38.601
And I guess -- I don't know why
Buzzfeed --

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:42.901
I guess if you work for
Buzzfeed, let us know why...

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:45.400
why you chose this terrible
photo of me.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:50.634
And, you know, actually,
a similar thing happened to me.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.234
[ Laughs ]

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:59.934
People were tagging me
about my birthday --

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:03.300
on my birthday on social media.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:08.267
It was like, "Oh, happy birthday
to comedian Tig Notaro."

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:11.701
And it was a picture of
Rosie O'Donnell.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:14.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.200
And I was just like, "What?
They just like --

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.901
It's like, 'oh, national lesbian
birthday'?"

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.501
And just --

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:27.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.667
-Is that a thing?

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:32.901
-They just Google, like,
any lesbian with short hair.

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.067
And they're like, "That's fine."
-Yeah.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.634
-"Whatever."
Just Melissa Etheridge.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.367
Anybody -- She doesn't have
short hair, but anyway.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:45.868
-Can we talk about your new --
You're a movie star now.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.968
-I am.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.701
-I've actually been a movie star
for a while.

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:51.234
-Yeah, that's true.
For a while now.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.567
-For a while.
-Are you enjoying the fame?

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:56.934
-I enjoy my level of fame
because...

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:59.467
Well, I guess there's a downside
because I --

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:02.434
You know, I do stand-up and I'll
tour around the country.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.634
I did a 70-city tour last year.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:10.567
And sometimes, I knock on
the back door of the theater,

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.434
and security won't let me in.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.400
-And you're playing there
that night?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.634
-Yeah. I'm there that night.
And they're like, "Uh, yeah?"

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:24.334
And I'm like, "Oh, I'm
performing at the show."

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.434
-"At the show here tonight."

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.601
At your show.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:32.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:36.367
Yeah. And I have to -- I have to
explain that I am

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.133
the big sensation that sold out
the theater.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.801
-Yeah. Well, got to kind of keep
you humble.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:42.267
Got to keep you moving,
on your toes.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:43.734
-Yeah.
-Yeah, because you can't let

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.367
this movie star status
go to your head.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:49.067
-I know. And just having
my birthday wishes have

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.868
Rosie O'Donnell's face, like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:54.601
-I want to talk about this
movie, "Your Place or Mine."

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.200
We just had Ashton Kutcher
on the show yesterday.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.234
He was singing your --
-He's a dream boat.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.334
-Singing your praises.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.200
It's you, Ashton Kutcher,
Reese Witherspoon.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.634
This is exactly a rom-com
that I want to watch.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.367
-Yes.
-That I want to see.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:11.601
What's it like being in
a rom-com with these two?

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:17.300
-Well, it's really fun.
And they're both so great.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:23.634
I will say it was a little
alarming to watch the movie

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:28.434
because during the filming, I'm
thinking, "Oh, this is so great.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.968
Everybody's so nice and fun."

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:34.767
And then I'm watching
the actual movie,

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:39.534
and these two people are
so attractive, Reese and Ashton.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:42.434
And I'm not --
Look, I'm not hard on myself.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:47.067
But I will say it was alarming.

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:51.434
You see these beautiful Ashton
and Reese faces on screen,

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.300
and I play their friend.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.634
And I come around a corner,

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.901
and I was startled.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.701
I look like I'm the same age
as Yoda.

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.300
[ Applause ]

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.601
-What?

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:10.267
No.
-No. Wait.

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:13.634
Listen. And I'm truly --
I'm not hard on myself.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.968
But I was like [Gasps]
"Oh, my gosh."

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:22.267
I mean, we have very different,
you know, night lotion regimen.

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:23.300
What do you --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.968
I don't know what's going on.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.834
But I was just like, "Whoa!"

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:29.367
-How do we set up the movie?

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.200
-How do we set it up?
-Yeah.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.000
-Well, it's a rom-com.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.234
-Yep.
-Starring Reese Witherspoon...

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:41.000
...Ashton Kutcher and Yoda --
-No --

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.400
[ Laughter ]
Alright, alright, alright.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.267
It's very funny. And I want to
show everyone a clip.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.601
Here's Tig Notaro
and Reese Witherspoon

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:50.200
in "Your Place or Mine."
Take a look at this.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.767
-Have you been looking at
her Instagram?

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:54.467
-You think I'm not gonna be
looking at

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:56.801
Jimmy's girlfriend's
Instagram account?

00:06:56.801 --> 00:07:00.100
I mean, what are we even doing?
Who would I even be?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.767
-Look, it's fine. It works
for him. It works for me.

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:04.567
And besides, Jack loves hanging
out with Scarlet.

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.234
-Alright. Well, I hope that you

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.734
get what you want
out of this trip.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.567
-Yes.
-And what you need.

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:13.067
You know, get your degree,
find a man, come home.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:15.534
And then remodel that
ancient kitchen of yours.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:18.200
I also think it's time to get
layers in your hair.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.801
Layers, but not bangs.

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:22.100
Bangs are for an emergency.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.834
-That's right!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:27.434
Tig Notaro.
"Your Place or Mine" begins

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:29.234
streaming this Friday
on Netflix.

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:30.634
We'll be right back
with a performance

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:33.467
from Fitz and the Tantrums.
Stick around!

